{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21717 - PROTEIN:2333",
  "verbalization": "Ligustrone A is shown to have a target relationship with Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3 through multiple pathways, with the highest confidence scores in Path 1 and Path 2. These pathways indicate that Ligustrone A acts on HCT-8, which is targeted by 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, a compound that in turn targets Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3. This suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3, which is a key enzyme in the ADP-ribosyltransferase family. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent involvement of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol as a mediator supports a mechanistic link between Ligustrone A and the enzyme. The evidence is further strengthened by the shared pathway involving HCT-8 and Conferol, which also leads to the same target. The integration of these pathways implies that Ligustrone A may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of this enzyme, potentially through the action of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol. The evidence is consistent and supports a plausible biological mechanism, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
